  "title": "First Buddhist Council",
  "summary": "According to tradition, Buddhist monks gathered at Rajagaha (Rajgir) under King Ajatashatru's patronage, with Mahakassapa presiding, to preserve the Buddha's teachings and monastic rules after his death. Tradition has it meeting three months after his parinibbana and finishing in seven months; the 483 BCE date is traditional.",
